Date: Mon, 27 Apr 2026 00:43:23 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 07/22] Per-session inbox with deferred delivery

Adds POST /session/:sessionID/inbox and an in-memory SessionInbox queue
so a chat message can be delivered to a session that's currently
mid-turn. Existing /message and /prompt_async still throw BusyError on
busy sessions; /inbox always accepts and queues if needed.

Mechanism:
  - SessionInbox (packages/opencode/src/session/inbox.ts) keeps a
    Map<SessionID, PromptInput[]> with FIFO semantics. enqueueOrSend()
    checks SessionRunState.assertNotBusy and either fires
    SessionPrompt.prompt fire-and-forget (idle path) or pushes onto the
    queue (busy path). A re-queue fallback handles the rare race where
    a runner appears between assertNotBusy and the prompt call.
  - SessionRunState's onIdle hook now calls SessionInbox.drainNext, so
    the next queued message dispatches as soon as the current turn
    completes. drainNext is fire-and-forget; it re-enters
    SessionPrompt.prompt which re-arms a fresh runner for the session.
  - New BusEvent session.message.queued (with { sessionID, depth })
    propagates over SSE so subscribers (TUI, MCP clients) can show a
    pending-inbox indicator.
  - Route confirms the session exists via Session.get before queueing
    so unknown IDs surface as 404 instead of silently disappearing.

Hivemind uses /inbox from its cross-session MCP tools (send_to_main,
send_to_session) so a subagent can ping the orchestrator while the
orchestrator is still blocked inside the Task call that spawned it.
The orchestrator picks up the queued message on the very next idle.

